2026-05-05T00:00Z claude created

--- body ---
Cosmetic Go changes to improve consistency of user-facing output:

- check.go: WARNING → WARN prefix (align with stray-source warning style)
- close.go: ALREADY_CLOSED → CLOSED (already) (matches status verb pattern)
- check.go: inline plural — "1 warning" / "2 warnings" (no more (s) fake plural)
- validate.go: inline plural — "1 file" / "2 files"
- init.go: %t → yes/no booleans in Applied: section output
- init.go: "AGENTS.md pointer" → "AGENTS.md entry" in plan and output lines
- init.go: "manifest:" → "manifest written:" for clarity
- validate.go: "preamble" → "header section" in error messages

Exit criteria:
- No WARNING in check.go
- No ALREADY_CLOSED in source
- No (s) fake-plural in format strings
- No preamble in validate.go error messages
- No %t in init.go Printf calls
